title The bound decided one room over -- Tablecloth's derived content budget, and the derivation read as its own fact
prompt The standing Silence seat: open on ListAgents and the cold roster, reds first, then the infrastructure half of Grain in Glow -- the vanes and services.
think Opened on ListAgents (one peer, grain-c0, interactive) and a fetch of xy that read level, so nothing to rebase and no peer file in flight. Reds first read clean: construction/REDS.md holds one row, zero OPEN, so the constructive queue was genuinely open.
think The cold roster ran 94 guards to 89 green, 5 red, tree_at_open equal to tree_at_close -- rule_twin is gate %7, width_check is another body's, the two Pond rows are Hush's, and remember_git_nib is this card's nib lagging HEAD, which this round's own commit closes. No new red, so no standfast.
think Rota row 2 by N=3787 mod 5 -- Fire, the row that sees: the threshold page plus standfast, reds-first, and the three depths of removal. Fire's lap looks hard at what refuses, so this lap spent its care on the control rather than on the desk.
think My own last lap named the continuation: Tablecloth's max_name, its max_content_bytes, and its eight ClothError paths each wanting a pedestal. Crux-first picked max_content_bytes, because it is the only one of the three whose number its own module never spells -- brushstroke/tablecloth.rye declares `pub const max_content_bytes: u32 = beading.max_resin_bytes;`, so mantra/beading.rye decides the value at 512 and tablecloth only names it.
think That makes the derivation a THIRD reading beside the two values. Respell tablecloth's line as a literal 512 and every number in the tree still agrees, while the sentence the desk makes -- the artifact budget follows the resin budget -- has quietly become false; the next honest raise of max_resin_bytes would then move one room and leave the other behind with nothing to say so. So the scan greps the derivation itself rather than inferring it from agreement.
think One guard rather than two. tools/fixtures/t/tablecloth_glow_tend_scan.sh was already named for the vane rather than for one desk, so the second pedestal widened it -- two shared helpers (placard_of, example_of), five new readings, and content-prefixed verdicts so a single verdict line still names which room refused. A second parallel guard family would have been a lantern firing twice.
obs The control is where the design is actually proven. Nineteen cases in a throwaway pen holding the four files the scan reads: sixteen refusals, and three welcomes. The third welcome is the one that matters -- max_resin_bytes raised to 1024 in mantra/beading.rye and the pedestal following, with brushstroke/tablecloth.rye untouched because it never held the value, walking free. An elder Tend witness would red there, since it pins the literal a third time inside the guard.
obs The catalog readings are decided before the content readings on purpose, so a fault in the elder pedestal names itself rather than hiding behind a younger one. Case 14 is the crux proven from its own side: derivation respelled as a literal, every number still agreeing, verdict derivation_broken.
obs No new roster row. The guard already holds its seat at tier cadence, so the widening cost the roster a comment block rather than a row -- 113 rows and 19 at cadence, unchanged.
obs The first hot pass read 88 green and 6 red, the sixth being geode_libraries: adding a module to src/shape moves docs-geode/libraries/README.md, which is generated. The card already names the pre-commit hook as the regenerator, so the red was expected rather than a defect -- yet a hot green is supposed to measure the tree the commit ships, so the index was regenerated (one line: the shape room 31 -> 32), staged, and the whole roster re-run to 89 green with the same five reds the cold pass carried.
obs A second, smaller thing surfaced while opening the new day shelf: session-logs/README.md claimed 22 rows for 20260829 and 64 for 20260828 where the shelves hold 76 and 66. Counted rather than remembered, corrected in place, and session-logs/CHAPTERS.md -- whose last row was 20260827 -- takes the three missing shelf rows. A count carried in prose drifts the first lap nobody edits both, which is the ledger headline's own lesson one room over.
